<Base title="Contact" description="Contact Talha M Blog: email contact@talhablog.com for corrections, right of reply, copyright and privacy requests, feedback and story suggestions.">
  <section class="article-head"><h1>Contact</h1></section>
  <div class="prose">
    <p><em>Last updated: October 15, 2026</em></p>

    <p>Thank you for wanting to reach us. Talha M Blog is a small, independent website, and email is the best and fastest way to contact us. Whether you found a mistake in a story, want to suggest a topic, or simply want to say hello, we are happy to hear from you.</p>

    <h2>Our email address</h2>
    <p><a href="mailto:contact@talhablog.com"><b>contact@talhablog.com</b></a></p>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:contact@talhablog.com?subject=Message%20for%20Talha%20M%20Blog">Tap here to write an email</a>
    </p>
    <p>Please write a clear subject line — for example "Correction", "Copyright", "Privacy" or "Story suggestion" — so we can understand at once what your email is about and answer the most urgent ones first.</p>

    <h2>What you can write to us about</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Corrections:</b> If you find a mistake in any article — a wrong date, a wrong name, an old figure, anything — please tell us which article it is in (copy the link of the page if you can) and what should be corrected. We will check it against reliable sources, fix it if it is wrong, and mark the article as updated. Honest corrections make this website better for every reader, and we are thankful for them.</li>
      <li><b>Right of reply:</b> If a story is about you or your organisation and you believe something in it is wrong, incomplete or unfair, write to us with your response. Where it is fair, we will correct the story or add your response to it, so readers can see both sides.</li>
      <li><b>Feedback:</b> Tell us what you liked, what was hard to understand, or what you want to see more of. Because our promise is simple English for everyone, feedback about difficult words or confusing parts is especially useful.</li>
      <li><b>Story suggestions:</b> You can suggest a topic you want explained in simple English — a news story, a famous person's life, a new phone, an AI tool, a sports record. We cannot promise to write every suggested topic, but good suggestions are read carefully and often become future posts.</li>
      <li><b>Questions about a post:</b> If something in a story is unclear, ask us and we will try to explain it or update the post so it becomes clearer for everyone.</li>
      <li><b>Copyright and takedown requests:</b> If you believe that something on this website — text or an image — uses your material without permission, write to us following the steps in the next section. Copyright messages are checked on priority.</li>
      <li><b>Privacy requests:</b> You can ask us to delete a comment you posted, to remove your email from the newsletter list (you can also use the unsubscribe link in any newsletter email), or to delete other information connected with you. Write with the subject "Privacy" and tell us which comment or email address it concerns. How we handle information is explained in our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
      <li><b>Comments help:</b> If your comment does not appear, or you want your own comment removed, email us the link of the story and the name you commented with, and we will look into it.</li>
      <li><b>Technical problems:</b> If a page does not open, an image does not load, or installing the website as an app does not work on your device, tell us what device and browser you are using and what you saw, and we will try to fix it.</li>
      <li><b>Business and advertising:</b> For genuine business questions, write to the same email address with "Business" in the subject line. Please note that we never accept payment to change, hide or remove a news story.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to send a copyright request</h2>
    <p>So that we can act quickly, please include these things in your email:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your full name, and the name of the owner of the material if that is not you.</li>
      <li>The exact link (URL) of the page on talhablog.com where the material appears.</li>
      <li>A short description of the material that belongs to you, and where it was first published, if you can share that link.</li>
      <li>A simple statement that you own the material, or that you are authorised to act for the owner, and that the use on our website is not permitted.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We aim to reply to complete copyright requests within a few working days. If a request checks out, we will remove or correct the material as quickly as we reasonably can, and we will email you back when it is done. The same process is described in our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a>.</p>

    <h2>When will you get a reply?</h2>
    <p>We read every genuine email that arrives. This website is run by a very small team — in fact, by one person — so replies are not instant and can sometimes take a few days, especially when many messages arrive together. Corrections, right-of-reply and copyright messages are checked first, even if a personal reply takes longer. Please do not send the same message again and again; one clear email is enough, and it will be seen.</p>

    <h2>Please do not send</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Passwords, bank details, card numbers or any private financial information — we will never ask you for these, and no genuine message from this website will ever request them.</li>
      <li>Spam, chain messages or advertisements for unrelated products.</li>
      <li>Abusive or threatening messages. Honest criticism is welcome; abuse is deleted without a reply.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Other ways to follow us</h2>
    <p>New stories are published on this website regularly, and you can always find the latest posts on our <a href="/">homepage</a>. You can follow Talha M Blog on Instagram at <a href="https://www.instagram.com/talh_ablog" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@talh_ablog</a>, where we share our newest stories, and you can meet the writer and see all of his stories on our <a href="/author/">author page</a>. You can also subscribe to our free email newsletter on any story page, so new stories come to your inbox. For everything else — corrections, questions, suggestions and business — email remains the surest way to reach us.</p>

    <p>Thank you for reading, and thank you for writing. Readers who take the time to send a correction or a kind word are a big reason this small website keeps going.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
